        "verbatim": "Hello! I understand your concern about the alignment of session TUT-4411 with California's Common Core State Standards for 5th grade math. Let me first gather some information and then address your inquiry.\n\nI can see that session TUT-4411 was a 60-minute math session for 5th grade that took place on October 25, 2025. The session was marked as covering standards CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.5.NF.A.1 and CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.5.NF.B.3, which are indeed part of the 5th grade Common Core standards for fractions.\n\nLooking at the session summary, I can confirm your observation: \"Session focused on adding and subtracting fractions with unlike denominators using algorithmic methods. Covered least common denominators and cross-multiplication techniques. Limited use of visual models or real-world application examples.\"\n\nFor your reference, here are the appropriate EduTutor Pro resources aligned with these California CCSS standards:\n\n1. **5th Grade Math: Fractions with Visual Models** (CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.5.NF.A.1)\n   - Interactive Worksheet: https://edututorpro.com/resources/5nf-a1\n\n2. **Real-World Fraction Applications** (CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.5.NF.B.3)\n   - Video Tutorial: https://edututorpro.com/resources/5nf-b3\n\n3. **California Standards Alignment Guide**\n   - PDF Guide: https://edututorpro.com/resources/ca-math-standards\n\nTo better assist you and determine the appropriate next steps, could you please provide your user ID? This will help me understand your membership tier and access any additional information about this session.\n\nBased on our policy, tutor performance complaints should be escalated to human academic coordinators. If you'd like to file a formal complaint about the instructional approach used in this session, I can help facilitate that transfer once I have your user information.",
